"Enuff", yelled Bert the Troll, but of course there were no trolls about.
Zan stopped by at the lightstore. "Salutations, shopkeeper! 
Understand that you are a strong candidate for the future mayorship
of Minetown." The shopkeeper, Izchak was not impressed. He
managed to send a small tingle of anger up Zan's spinal cord
by smiling and shaking his head slowly. But he also said:
"Aye, and you might thrive by rendering services here."
Irritated, Zan left the Minetown.

After some K-18 (sax and violins, what did you expect)
encounters, Zan decided to take the fight to the demons. A lone
Castle, filled with humans, stood guarding the Valley of the Dead.
Zan made short work of the "guardians" only to discover that the
Castle didn't try to prevent anything from going in the Valley.
The Castle was probably erected to keep the undead where they 
belonged. As Zan reluctantly jumped through a trap door, she
understood why. The Valley was filled with things that should not see the
daylight. At least, that is what the consensus of Law said. The dead
are indeed poor masters, but what great workers they would make.
Surely the royal embalmers would work out a solution which would
satisfy the ever-growing kingdoms' needs. But these lich mages
are too powerful, greedy without goals. They must be put to rest!
Even after the dreadful liches were dust, Zan flinched as she
saw a healer corpse spontaneously spring to life... for a moment.

Zan went forth, and soon perished Asmodeus and Baalzebub,
both powerful demons. They didn't appreciate their one zorkmid
bribes. Stormbringer seemed disinterested in the demons' odd
matter, but all the more viciously did Zan's unnamed silver saber
bite the demons.

Upon reaching a swamp, Zan felt weary, so she filled her bottles
with swamp water. Manannan Mac Lir would turn them holy.
And behold, on level 15 altar he did so, and dropped a silver
saber named Werebane on the altar. "Gosh, thanks." //The usual comment
//Later, Ogresmasher was created in a similiar way.

But what happened at the Camelot Castle shortly after that?
Having already vanquished a knight, Zan brought her blades
down on her former comrades. 

In no time Zan was back in... Hell. Yes, it seemed like Hell. Only
the most cunning and influential baddies would seek sanctuary
in Hell... or anywhere beneath it. Still, the majority of the lost souls
were not seen by Zan. Perhaps this so-called Gehennom was
merely a physical extension of the greater Hell ? Think of it,
if Hell isn't a totally hopeless place (for Zan placed her hope on
her weapons and skills), then is Heaven such a great place, then?
In any case, a trapper ate up Moloch's priest. Burrrp!

"40 levels deep, Keep of Orcus.
Infernal band, a fiendish circus.
Let me pass! We did not discuss.
Prince would weep. For a wand;
not for nothing, such a fuss."

On level 44 Zan found a Dragonbane. Oh well, more decor to the
demigoddess palace, then.

Level fourty-seven was the Vibrating Square. After an invocation
ritual, a path was revealed into Moloch's sanctum. But where
is the devil himself ? Ah, he has left a high priest in charge of 
business. Needless to mention, a fight ensued.
Both living and dead fell, and Zan snatched the Amulet and
started the long journey up. 

"Earth, air, fire, water!
Can you stop Manannan's daughter?
Not your blades, nor your will,
Way of chivalry could her kill.

But Lugh, you lost your grip.
Many a cry did you ignore.
Chaos god will fill his ship,
Law is but a drunkman's lore."

Astral Plane, at last! A guardian angel of Manannan Mac Lir
appeared. Despite Zan's adventures, it appeared bored.
Lazily it would help Zan in battle, but it didn't matter. 
In any case, the angel wanted to survive, and so it did.
After clearing the temples from spiritual enemies and strange
adventurers, Zan returned to the middle temple and offered
the Amulet to Manannan Mac Lir. Fumbling with the Amulet,
Zan lost the control of her sword once more. An angel perished,
and the high priest of Manannan Mac Lir was angered.
"All the more for me, then..."



